# Flow 2, Esc back and reopen: a note of the vault opens in the preview (the default), Edit, a line typed, Esc at once
# (before the autosave): the save on the way back; opened again it shows the line; Ctrl+P finds it by name; with the
# setting "Open notes in: Editor" it opens in the editor; the header's Esc saves too.
seed vault
wait 900
tap "All notes"
tap "All notes"
wait 400
tap "Deck build log"
tap "Deck build log"
wait 500
expect state page preview
key ctrl-e
wait 400
expect state page editor
key ctrl-end
key enter
type Reopened on the deck.
key esc
wait 400
expect state page folder
expect state last_save ok
expect file "Deck build log.md" contains "three screws. Notes from the forum: <https://example.org/hinge>\n\nReopened on the deck."
shot 01-back-in-folder
key enter
wait 500
expect state page preview
expect state note "Deck build log.md"
key end
wait 200
expect span "Reopened on the deck."
shot 02-reopened
key esc
wait 300
key esc
wait 300
# by name
key ctrl-p
wait 300
type deck bu
wait 200
expect state sel_id create
key down
expect state sel_id "note:Deck build log.md"
shot 03-by-name
key enter
wait 500
expect state page preview
expect state depth 2
key esc
wait 300
# Settings > Open notes in: Editor
key end
key enter
wait 300
key down
key down
key enter
wait 300
expect state popup choice
key right
key enter
wait 300
expect state open_in editor
key esc
wait 300
key ctrl-p
type shopping list
key enter
wait 500
expect state page editor
expect state note "Shopping list.md"
type Added.
wait 100
# the header's Esc saves and goes back
tap "Esc"
wait 500
expect state page home
expect file "Shopping list.md" contains "Added.# Shopping list"
